{
  "id": "vilar-sequestration-oscillator-second-biology",
  "name": "Vilar promoter-binding and protein-sequestration oscillator",
  "description": "Deterministic nine-state model retains both promoter occupancies and sequestration. It does not simulate intrinsic noise or establish noise resistance; distinct from a three-gene repressilator and Hill-function clock models. All15 rates and nine initial states follow the original Fig1 caption. Time is hours and cellular volume is unity. Horizon60 and Radau outputstep0.1 are our choices. https://computableplant.ics.uci.edu/emj/classes/277C_04/papers/networks/villar_barkai.pdf Signed net-rate flows encode the stated differential equations. No clamps or resets. These educational equations are not fitted biological forecasts.",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.092133899",
  "reference": "Vilar, Kueh, Barkai and Leibler (2002), Mechanisms of noise-resistance in genetic oscillators, PNAS99:5988-5992, Eq1 and Fig1 caption.",
